/// A value that one task at a time reads and updates inside `Mutex.with_lock`. The first part of
/// the cell is the lock word of the runtime; `Mutex.create` makes it free. The value is not Copy
/// and no function value can capture it. The cell lives in the buffer of `cell`, so a borrow of
/// the mutex stays valid however the record is moved.
record Mutex<'a> { cell: [(i32u * 'a)] }
